# Every path is the same file: this is a single-page app, and the router
# decides what to draw. Without it, /reset — the address a password link
# lands on — is a 404 from the host, and the person who clicked it is told
# the page does not exist.
#
# 200, not 301: the browser must keep the URL it asked for, or the router
# never sees which screen was wanted.
#
# Routes are one segment deep on purpose. index.html references its assets
# relatively (base './', so Capacitor can serve from disk in phase 5), and
# "./assets/x.js" resolves correctly from /reset but not from /a/b.
/*  /index.html  200
